    "https://www.clayton.edu/career/index.php": {
      "title": "Career and Professional Development",
      "description": "Career and Professional Development - Clayton State University Skip to Content We use cookies to give you the best experience and to help improve our website. For more information see our Privacy Notice . Questions or requests, please complete our DSR form . Ok Toggle navigation LochNet Directory Giving Apply Search on Desktop Search on mobile About About Home Visit Us History & Traditions Fast Facts Work at CSU Office of the President Administration Community Outreach Contact Us Academics Academics Home Undergraduate Study Degrees, Majors & Certificates Graduate Study Colleges & Schools Academic Affairs Academic Catalog Course Search Course Syllabi Academic Resources Online Learning Faculty Members' Profiles Admissions Admissions Home Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Orientation Continuing Education Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Forms Request Information Student Life Student Life Home Arts & Culture Books & Dining Campus Technology Career and Professional Development Care Center Community, Belonging & Veterans Center Dean of Students Health & Wellness Lakers Care & Share Parents Student Care & Support Student Engagement Transportation & Parking Services University Housing Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Events Get Involved Stay Connected Alumni Benefits Membership Laker Pride Alumni Giving Contact Alumni Career and Professional Development Toggle navigation Students Career Assessment Type Career Development Checklist Career Exploration Career and Professional Development Events Employer Information Session Graduate School Information Internship Information Job Fair Information Job Search Information Laker CareerZone On-Campus Recruiting & Interviewing Presentation Request Form Stepping Blocks Student Worker Guidelines What can I do with my Major? Workshops Employers Career Fair Information Employer Information Sessions Employer Policies Internship Information Job Posting Information On-Campus Recruiting & Interviewing Program and Student Facts Travel Information Alumni & Families Employer Information Session Events Families Graduate School Information Job Fair Information Job Search Information Laker Career Mentoring Program On-Campus Recruiting & Interviewing Career Outcomes Faculty & Staff Alternative to Canceling Class Career Counseling Guidelines for Student Workers Online Career Guide Contact Us While at Clayton State, your job is to explore. To discover your strengths and define\n                     what you want to do with them. To seize opportunities that come your way. Our job\n                     in Career and Professional Development is to help make all of that possible for you. At every stage of your college career, we provide the resources you need for success\n                     both during your time here and in your professional life after graduation. From resume\n                     building and interview guidance to career fairs, internships and career coaching,\n                     there is no shortage of pathways to making your dream real. Let’s get started! Laker CareerZone Utilize this career management system to discover new job, internship, work study\n                                       opportunities and register for workshops/events! Student Login (Upload your résumé and apply for jobs!) Recruiter Login Post jobs and register for events! Resume Review The Office of Career and Professional Development resume reviews are on Tuesdays from\n                                          2–4 p.m. and Wednesdays from 10 a.m.–2 p.m. on Microsoft Teams, or in-person Edgewater\n                                          Hall, Suite 228. Book a Resume Review Session Upcoming Events Sep 8 Resume Review Sep 9 Resume Review Sep 14 Internship Week Kick-Off Sep 15 Resume Review Sep 15 Internship Job Search Strategies Workshop Sep 16 Internship Networking Breakfast Internships Information Internships integrate knowledge and theory learned in the classroom with practical\n                                          application and skills development in a professional setting. Internships give students\n                                          the opportunity to gain valuable applied experience and make connections in professional\n                                          fields they are considering for career paths; and give employers the opportunity to\n                                          guide and evaluate talent. Students Employers Career Exploration Career Decisions Clayton State Majors and Related Careers Interests Personality Skills and Abilities Salary Career Decisions Learn More Steppingblocks Steppingblocks is an online career exploration platform. Students, faculty, and staff\n                                          have access to a 20-question personality assessment, a career path explorer, an institutional\n                                          outcomes explorer, and a tuition analyzer. Learn more about Steppingblocks Online Career Guide This online resource is full of tips, advice and samples regarding career assessments,\n                                       job search strategies, resume and cover letter development, interviewing, social media\n                                       and dressing for success. View the Career Guide Laker Link Career MENTORING PROGRAM Our program directors work with you to make sure that you take the courses you need\n                                       for your degree plan. They’re experts at navigating program-completion requirements\n                                       and can help keep you on track as you work toward graduation. Learn More Career Videos Thousands of videos! Industry professionals sharing their job descriptions, backgrounds\n                                          and preparation advice. “Get Hired” advice videos on interviewing, resume writing,\n                                          and many more topics to help you land that job! Learn More Big Interview Use Big Interview video and virtual tutorial to develop and practice interviewing\n                                          skills with unlimited interview practice sessions. Learn More Professional Clothing Closet The Professional Clothing Closet provides a way for Clayton State University students\n                                       to access FREE professional attire appropriate for career fairs, interviews, and the\n                                       workplace. Inventory includes suits, blazers, skirts, button-down shirts, and more.\n                                       Our goal is to help students look their best throughout their job search so they can\n                                       make a positive impression as they enter the professional world! Clothing Donations: Transform Your Closet Cleaning into Life-Changing Opportunities! Contact us for more\n                                          information on your planned donation. Email Career and Professional Development Corporate Partners View the Corporate Partners Student Spotlight Michelle Roache Learn More Berquila Arnold Learn More Share Your Story prev next Contact Career and Professional Development Location: Edgewater Hall, Suite 228 Phone: (678) 466-5400 Fax: (678) 466-5468 Email: Email Career and Professional Development Office Hours: Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.–5 p.m. Meet the Staff Find Your Major Apply Accreditation Strategic Plan Contact Us Public Safety Visitor Information Parking 2000 Clayton State Boulevard Morrow, GA 30260 (678) 466-4000 Maps & Directions Clayton State University Facebook Clayton State University Twitter Clayton State University Instagram Clayton State University YouTube Clayton State University LinkedIn A-Z index Calendar Laker Newsroom Offices/Depts Employment Title IX Anti-Hazing Accessibility 2000 Clayton State Boulevard Morrow, GA 30260 (678) 466-4000 Clayton State University Facebook Clayton State University Twitter Clayton State University Instagram Clayton State University YouTube Clayton State University LinkedIn © Clayton State University A Senior Unit of the University System of Georgia Ethics & Integrity Human Trafficking Notice Equal Opportunity Privacy ©"
    },
    "https://www.clayton.edu/about/administration/student-affairs/dean-of-students/index.php": {
      "title": "Dean of Students",
      "description": "Dean of Students - Clayton State University Skip to Content We use cookies to give you the best experience and to help improve our website. For more information see our Privacy Notice . Questions or requests, please complete our DSR form . Ok Toggle navigation LochNet Directory Giving Apply Search on Desktop Search on mobile About About Home Visit Us History & Traditions Fast Facts Work at CSU Office of the President Administration Community Outreach Contact Us Academics Academics Home Undergraduate Study Degrees, Majors & Certificates Graduate Study Colleges & Schools Academic Affairs Academic Catalog Course Search Course Syllabi Academic Resources Online Learning Faculty Members' Profiles Admissions Admissions Home Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Orientation Continuing Education Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Forms Request Information Student Life Student Life Home Arts & Culture Books & Dining Campus Technology Career and Professional Development Care Center Community, Belonging & Veterans Center Dean of Students Health & Wellness Lakers Care & Share Parents Student Care & Support Student Engagement Transportation & Parking Services University Housing Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Events Get Involved Stay Connected Alumni Benefits Membership Laker Pride Alumni Giving Contact Alumni Return to Top of Page Dean of Students The Dean of Students Office promotes student success, well-being, belonging, and persistence\n                                 by providing holistic support, advocacy, care coordination, accessibility services,\n                                 and behavioral intervention. Through collaborative partnerships and student-centered\n                                 practices, the office empowers students to navigate challenges, access resources,\n                                 and thrive academically, personally, and professionally. Care Referral Grievance Procedures Red Folder Welcome Message from the Dean of Students Hey Lakers! We’re so glad you’re here. As your Dean of Students, I want you to know this: you are not alone on this journey.\n                                 Our faculty, staff, and administrators are all deeply invested in your success. Whether\n                                 you’re adjusting to college life or getting closer to graduation, we’re here to support\n                                 you every step of the way. Don’t hesitate to reach out. We mean that. At Clayton State, we believe education should be a launchpad for social mobility,\n                                 a way to create new opportunities for yourself, your family, and your future. But\n                                 that kind of transformation doesn’t happen in isolation. I challenge you to stay connected,\n                                 stay engaged, and stay curious. Get involved. There’s something here for everyone. Take a stroll down Main Street\n                                 on the second floor of the University Center to feel the buzz of happenings or visit\n                                 the Student Activities Center to take care of your physical wellness at your very\n                                 own campus gym, just to name a few engagement opportunities. If you ever feel out\n                                 of the loop, check your Clayton State email and visit clayton.edu/calendar to stay\n                                 up to date on campus events, programs, and opportunities. And if you don’t see what\n                                 you’re looking for, that’s the beauty of being a Laker. This is a campus of possibility.\n                                 You have the power to create something new. This is your time. Let’s make it count together. Dr. Mya Richardson-Echols Staff Dr. Mya Richardson-Echols Dean of Students Email Mya Dr. Sarah Ray Assistant Dean of Students Email Sarah Mr. Mathew Trice, MPA Student Support Coordinator Email Matthew Contact Information Office Location James M. Baker University Center UC 250 Office Email Dean of Students Email Address Office Phone (678) 466-5444 Students by the Numbers 67% percentage of first-gen students 175 number of students supported 150 number of pantry visitors Services CARE Team The Care Team reviews reports of concerning behavior to ensure early intervention\n                                          and support. Our goal is to promote campus safety and student well-being through proactive,\n                                          coordinated responses. Get CARE Support Disability Services Located within Care & Support, Disability Services is here to help ensure students\n                                          with documented disabilities can access the necessary resources through a welcoming\n                                          and inclusive environment to make their dreams real. Explore Disability Services Care Center The Care Center provides individualized assistance to students facing personal, academic,\n                                          or financial challenges that may impact their college experience. Our team connects\n                                          students to campus and community resources to promote well-being and help them stay\n                                          on track. Discover the Care Center Community, Belonging & Veterans Center The CBVC is a place for Veterans and Active Duty members alike to meet, get information,\n                                          and just hang out and be themselves with like-minded individuals. Community & Veterans Info Support Students Through Giving Want to Donate to the Student Emergency Fund? Giving options are available year round. Give to Support Students First-Generation Our First-Generation College Student Support initiatives are designed to help students\n                                          navigate college life with confidence and community. First-Gen Resources Lakers Care and Share Lakers Care & Share is a cross-campus advisory council developed to help students\n                                          who are struggling with food and housing insecurity and having other essential needs. Explore Lakers Care & Share Find Your Major Apply Accreditation Strategic Plan Contact Us Public Safety Visitor Information Parking 2000 Clayton State Boulevard Morrow, GA 30260 (678) 466-4000 Maps & Directions Clayton State University Facebook Clayton State University Twitter Clayton State University Instagram Clayton State University YouTube Clayton State University LinkedIn A-Z index Calendar Laker Newsroom Offices/Depts Employment Title IX Anti-Hazing Accessibility 2000 Clayton State Boulevard Morrow, GA 30260 (678) 466-4000 Clayton State University Facebook Clayton State University Twitter Clayton State University Instagram Clayton State University YouTube Clayton State University LinkedIn © Clayton State University A Senior Unit of the University System of Georgia Ethics & Integrity Human Trafficking Notice Equal Opportunity Privacy ©"
    },
    "https://careers.hprod.onehcm.usg.edu/psc/careers/CAREERS/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=28000": {
      "title": "Clayton State University Careers",
      "description": "Careers Skip to Main Content Press Control+M to start dragging object ptnbsid=FIWjingY3a9g5SK4GBrJ%2b8OfrS0%3d Back Clayton State University Careers Search Category Name Search keywords Search in... Menu Category All Company Directory Job Data No results to display Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Actions Search My Preferences Help Sign Out Clayton State University Careers More Actions Welcome Sign In New User Thank you for your interest in employment at Clayton State University. You can search and review career opportunities from this page without creating an account. When you are ready to apply, log in or create a new applicant account, and you will be able to: View all career opportunities. Search specific criteria to find careers that interest you. Set up a search agent to notify you when positions are posted that match your search criteria. If you need any technical support or assistance completing an employment application, please don't hesitate to contact our dedicated USG Service Desk at (877) 251-2644 or support@usg.edu . For questions about positions at Clayton State University, please contact the Office of Human Resources at HumanResources@clayton.edu . Our applicant portal is designed to be accessible from a variety of devices, including desktops, laptops, and mobile devices. Due to an Oracle Known Issue, we recommend that Mac OS users browse and apply using a web browser other than Safari for the best experience. The University System of Georgia's and Clayton State University's policies on recruitment and selection, as well as Clayton State's Positions of Trust listing, can be found here: Resources & Policies - Clayton State University and https://www.usg.edu/hr/manual . Additionally, Clayton State University supports Freedom of Expression, as stated in our Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom policy, which can be found online at https://www.usg.edu/policymanual/section6/C2653 . The Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and the Higher Education Act (HEA) fire safety provisions require institutions of higher education to publish an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report. These reports include crime and fire statistics for the three most recently completed calendar years, institutional policies and procedures for reporting crimes, and current policies concerning the security of, and access to, campus facilities and residences, as well as security considerations in the maintenance of campus facilities.The reports are available online at: https://www.clayton.edu/public-safety/clery-act-and-crime-reporting/annual-security-and-crime-report . If you would like to retain a copy of the report, you may print it from your browser or request a paper copy by emailing the institution at humanresources@clayton.edu . View All Jobs My Job Notifications My Job Applications My Favorite Jobs My Saved Searches My Account Information Clayton State University Careers Sign In New User"
    },
